# RFC 5545 requires CRLF line endings. Git's autocrlf normalisation rewrites
# them to LF on commit, so the *served* file violated the spec even though the
# generated one did not -- Google tolerates LF, Apple Calendar and Outlook are
# stricter. -text stores these byte-for-byte as generated.
*.ics -text

# Shell and Python run on the Linux box. Git's autocrlf would hand a Windows
# clone CRLF copies, and a CRLF shebang line makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter literally named "bash\r" -- which fails with a message that
# points nowhere near the real cause.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
